# Portfolio security & hygiene

This repo is a **public personal portfolio**. Treat every commit as world-readable.

## Never commit
- `.env.local` or any real `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values that point to **internal** company systems (App Hub, Azure DevOps PATs, Key Vault, connection strings)
- Passwords, tokens, PATs, cookies, private keys (`*.pem`, `*.key`, `credentials.json`)
- Screenshots or exports that show live internal URLs, customer PHI, or employee PII beyond your own public profile
- CHI / Client Happiness Index product details (keep private)
- Duplicate or draft resume PDFs — only `public/KarunaVasu_Resume.pdf` (and optional ATS) belong in `public/`

## Safe to commit
- Portfolio source (`app/`), styles, public profile photo
- `.env.example` with **empty** placeholders only
- Public contact (email/GitHub/LinkedIn) you already show on the live site
- Case-study narrative and architecture at a high level (no hostnames, no secrets, no customer identifiers)

## Product demo URLs
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_BOTVETA_*` / `NEXT_PUBLIC_IVR_*` stay **env-only** with empty defaults in code
- Prefer case-study pages over linking to internal production App Hub

## Before every push
1. `git status` — no `.env.local`, no unexpected binaries
2. Confirm download resume is Software Engineer (`KarunaVasu_Resume.pdf`)
3. Do not force-push `main` unless explicitly requested
